WEBVTT

00:01:28.487 --> 00:01:31.413
which is generally
just a big cloud of birds.

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:35.907
And someone happened to catch
a quick video on their phone

00:01:35.931 --> 00:01:38.241
of these starlings flying.

00:01:38.265 --> 00:01:41.417
And at first, it's just an amorphous blob,

00:01:41.441 --> 00:01:44.393
and then there's a moment
where the birds shift,

00:01:44.417 --> 00:01:48.875
and they form the shape of a starling

00:01:48.899 --> 00:01:50.550
in the sky!

00:01:50.574 --> 00:01:51.583
(Laughter)

00:01:51.607 --> 00:01:53.630
And as soon as I saw it, I was like,

00:01:53.654 --> 00:01:56.057
(Gasps) "The universe has already
written the poem

00:01:56.081 --> 00:01:57.648
you were planning on writing!"

00:01:57.672 --> 00:01:58.752
(Laughter)

00:01:58.776 --> 00:02:02.066
Except, for the first time,
it didn't fill me with despair.